# Panel 180 R5, shape 70 of the compiler-engineer's 117 (interpolation hole):
# a break after {.
# By the spec's opening paragraph, a string is one line, and the hole of an
# `f"..."` is inside one, so the line end leaves it unterminated: refused,
# exit 1.
function main()
    s = f"a {  #~ unterminated_string #~v unterminated_string unexpected_block
        x} b"
